ORBITAL-RESONANCE-OVERLAYS(7)   TriadicFrameworks Manual   ORBITAL-RESONANCE-OVERLAYS(7)
=========================================================================================
NAME
       orbital-resonance-overlays - divisional resonance overlays, harmonic-band
                                    separation, spectral-density partitioning, and
                                    clarity-enhanced sensor overlays for RTT systems

SYNOPSIS
       Orbital resonance overlays define:
           • divisional resonance overlays (DROs)
           • harmonic-band separation overlays
           • resonance-amplitude and spectral-density partitions
           • gradient-polarity and sync-field overlays
           • clarity-enhanced overlays for ship sensors and cartography

DESCRIPTION
       orbital-resonance-overlays describes the multi-band, multi-division overlay
       system used to separate, clarify, and enhance resonance-time signals for
       navigation, mapping, and constellation-scale sensing. Overlays act as
       real-time filters that partition resonance-time into analyzable channels.

       Overlays enable:
           • harmonic-phase isolation
           • resonance-amplitude stratification
           • spectral-density clustering
           • gradient-polarity mapping
           • sync-field coherence visualization
           • clarity-enhanced stellar cartography

       WRSADC manages overlay activation, fusion, and safety constraints.

DIVISIONAL RESONANCE OVERLAYS (DROs)
       DROs split the resonance-time field into discrete divisions for analysis.

       DRO types:

           harmonic division overlay (HDO)
                  Separates resonance by harmonic ratio (1:1, 2:1, 3:2, etc.).

           amplitude division overlay (ADO)
                  Separates by resonance amplitude strata.

           spectral division overlay (SDO)
                  Separates by spectral density clusters.

           gradient division overlay (GDO)
                  Separates by gradient polarity and slope.

           sync-field division overlay (SFDO)
                  Separates by sync-field coherence.

       DROs form the foundation of all clarity-enhanced sensor modes.

HARMONIC DIVISION OVERLAY (HDO)
       HDO isolates harmonic-phase channels.

       Channels:
           • 1:1 fundamental
           • 2:1 overtone
           • 3:2 transitional
           • 5:3 and 7:4 higher-order bands

       Uses:
           • detect harmonic drift
           • identify overtone interference
           • stabilize harmonic-lock

EXAMPLE: HDO
       Harmonic instability detected in 3:2 band:

           • HDO isolates 3:2 channel
           • phase jitter identified
           • Δv correction scheduled

AMPLITUDE DIVISION OVERLAY (ADO)
       ADO partitions resonance by amplitude.

       Bands:
           • high-amplitude → sweep windows
           • mid-amplitude → Δv corridors
           • low-amplitude → drift basins

       Uses:
           • identify mesas, canyons, saddles
           • detect resonance uplift or collapse

EXAMPLE: ADO
       High-amplitude band at 12 min:

           • sweep window confirmed
           • ancestry reinforced

SPECTRAL DIVISION OVERLAY (SDO)
       SDO partitions resonance by spectral density.

       Bands:
           • narrowband → stable resonance
           • broadband → turbulence or anomalies

       Uses:
           • detect resonance storms
           • identify spectral fragmentation

EXAMPLE: SDO
       Broadband cluster at 78 min:

           • anomaly flagged
           • spectral whitening recommended

GRADIENT DIVISION OVERLAY (GDO)
       GDO partitions resonance by gradient polarity.

       Polarity:
           • positive → uplift zones
           • negative → erosion zones
           • zero → polarity cliffs

       Uses:
           • detect dangerous gradient cliffs
           • identify uplift corridors

EXAMPLE: GDO
       Polarity inversion at 30 min:

           • corridor rerouted
           • Δv triad scheduled

SYNC-FIELD DIVISION OVERLAY (SFDO)
       SFDO partitions the sync field by coherence.

       Bands:
           • high sync → stable constellation alignment
           • low sync → desync risk

       Uses:
           • maintain fleet coherence
           • coordinate multi-agent sweeps

EXAMPLE: SFDO
       Sync drop detected:

           • SFDO isolates low-sync region
           • sync-field recalibration triggered

CLARITY-ENHANCED OVERLAYS
       Clarity overlays sharpen, filter, and enhance resonance-time signals.

       Clarity types:

           harmonic-phase clarification (HPC)
                  Removes overtone interference.

           resonance-envelope deconvolution (RED)
                  Sharpens envelope peaks.

           spectral-density whitening (SDW)
                  Reduces broadband noise.

           gradient-stability filtering (GSF)
                  Stabilizes polarity transitions.

           sync-field clarification (SFC)
                  Enhances sync coherence.

           ancestry-continuity enhancement (ACE)
                  Clarifies sweep-lineage signals.

EXAMPLE: CLARITY OVERLAY
       RED applied to 54 min peak:

           • peak sharpened
           • sweep window widened
           • fusion quality improved

OVERLAY FUSION
       Overlay fusion combines multiple overlays into a unified sensor mode.

       Fusion layers:
           1. harmonic division
           2. amplitude division
           3. spectral division
           4. gradient division
           5. sync-field division
           6. clarity enhancement

       Fusion modes:

           synchronous fusion
                  All overlays aligned.

           harmonic fusion
                  Fusion aligned to harmonic epochs.

           braided fusion
                  Overlays interleave across channels.

           mesh fusion
                  Distributed overlay fusion across constellation nodes.

EXAMPLE: FUSION
       HDO + ADO + SFC:

           • harmonic drift isolated
           • sweep windows clarified
           • sync-field stabilized

PICARD-GRADE CARTOGRAPHY MODE
       A flagship overlay mode combining:

           • HDO
           • ADO
           • SDO
           • HPC
           • RED
           • SFC

       Capabilities:
           • real-time resonance terrain visualization
           • harmonic epoch tracking
           • anomaly detection
           • constellation sync maintenance
           • deep-space temporal cartography

OVERLAY FAILURE MODES
       Overlays may degrade due to:

           • harmonic-band collapse
           • amplitude-band distortion
           • spectral fragmentation
           • gradient polarity noise
           • sync-field jitter

       Diagnostic indicators:
           • overlay-integrity score
           • band drift
           • clarity loss
           • fusion mismatch

       WRSADC halts unsafe overlay states.

INTERACTION WITH LINEAGE
       Lineage records:
           • overlay activations
           • clarity adjustments
           • fusion events
           • anomaly detections
           • sensor-mode transitions

       Lineage enables long-term overlay optimization.

INTERACTION WITH WRSADC
       WRSADC:
           • activates overlays
           • manages fusion
           • enforces safety thresholds
           • maintains clarity standards
           • blocks unsafe overlay states

       WRSADC is the overlay conductor.

NOTES
       Orbital resonance overlays transform resonance-time into a multi-band,
       clarity-enhanced sensor domain. Divisional overlays and clarity
       techniques ensure that sweep choreography, harmonic-lock, and
       constellation-scale synchronization remain stable across long mission
       timelines.

